    "title": "No. 17 Arkansas Dominates South Carolina with 108-74 Victory",
    "text": "• No. 17 Arkansas defeated South Carolina 108-74 on Wednesday night.\n• Darius Acuff Jr. of Arkansas had 18 points and 13 assists.\n• Meleek Thomas led Arkansas with 21 points off the bench.\n• Malique Ewin scored 18 points for Arkansas.\n• Trevon Brazile had 13 points for Arkansas.\n• D.J. Wagner added 12 points for Arkansas.\n• Nick Pringle of Arkansas scored 15 points and grabbed seven rebounds.\n• Acuff, a freshman, recorded his third double-double and set a career-best for assists.\n• Acuff has scored in double figures in every game this season.\n• Meechie Johnson led South Carolina with 29 points.\n• Arkansas went on a 12-2 run to take a 22-12 lead.\n• South Carolina shot 1 of 9 from the field during that run.\n• Arkansas didn't commit its first turnover until 3:33 of the first half.\n• South Carolina had 10 turnovers, leading to 10 points for Arkansas.\n• Arkansas went on a 19-1 run in the second half.\n• Arkansas made seven straight field goals during the 19-1 run.\n• Arkansas's 34-point win tied for the sixth-largest in an SEC game in school history.\n• Arkansas's 108 points equaled its sixth-most in an SEC game.\n• South Carolina's record is 10-7, 1-3 in the Southeastern Conference.\n• Arkansas's record is 13-4, 3-1 in the Southeastern Conference.\n• South Carolina plays at Auburn on Saturday.\n• Arkansas visits No. 21 Georgia on Saturday.",
